---
import Atlas from '../layouts/Atlas.astro';
import RasterEvidence from '../components/RasterEvidence.astro';
import evidence from '../generated/evidence.json';
import { route } from '../scripts/routes.mjs';
import { metrics, modelKeys, percent } from '../scripts/metrics.mjs';

const { benchmark } = evidence;
const best = metrics(benchmark.models.dinov3.aggregate_confusion_matrix);
const exhibits = [
  ['01', 'Data Atlas', 'Trace the observed band mapping behind each channel name.', 'atlas'],
  ['02', 'Data Pipeline', 'Explore recorded crops and the training transformations.', 'pipeline'],
  ['03', 'Model Anatomy', 'Follow configured tensors through DINOv3 and the decoder.', 'models'],
  ['04', 'Evaluation Observatory', 'Connect confusion counts to documented scene crops.', 'evaluation'],
  ['05', 'Experiment Studio', 'Compare saved validation recipes and their controls.', 'experiments'],
  ['06', 'Evidence & Reproducibility', 'Trace configurations, checkpoints, and limitations.', 'methods'],
];
---
<Atlas>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Field notes / DeepNet research atlas</p>
        <h1>From Pixels<br />to <em>Proof.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">A research atlas for aerial semantic segmentation. Inspect recorded predictions, compare them with the reference, and trace every score to its experiment.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="#journey">Follow one crop <span>↓</span></a><a class="button secondary" href={route('evaluation')}>Open evaluation <span>↗</span></a></div>
        <p class="hero-caveat">A pixel-aligned excerpt from the source RGBIR scene, eroded reference, and two archived model outputs. The comparison is tied to its scene, coordinates, checkpoint hashes, and label protocol.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-plate">
        <RasterEvidence initialCase="4_14-4608-3584" context="Home" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="data-strip" aria-label="Potsdam benchmark at a glance">
    <div class="wrap strip-grid">
      <div class="strip-title"><span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Evidence snapshot</span><strong>ISPRS Potsdam</strong><a href={route('methods') + '#claim-001'}>Historical benchmark ↗</a></div>
      <div><strong>{benchmark.scene_ids.length}</strong><span>Benchmark scenes</span></div>
      <div><strong>{(best.total / 1e6).toFixed(2)}M</strong><span>Scored pixels · eroded reference</span></div>
      <div><strong>4</strong><span>Recorded model recipes</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap research-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> The research question</p>
    <div><h2>What does a segmentation score hide?</h2><p>DeepNet studies how spectral inputs, pretrained encoders, decoder choices, and sampling recipes shape urban land-cover predictions. Aggregate metrics describe the historical benchmark cohort; paired maps show where two recorded systems agree and diverge.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap journey" id="journey">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> One scene / one recorded crop</p><h2>Follow the evidence, layer by layer.</h2><p>The comparison above keeps one scene window fixed while you switch between archived RGB, reference, predictions, and paired outcomes. Its coordinates and model provenance stay attached to the selected crop.</p></div>
    <ol class="scene-stages">
      <li><span class="mono">01 / INPUT</span><h3>Optical view</h3><p>RGB display from the matched RGB cache. Potsdam ground sampling distance: 5 cm.</p></li>
      <li><span class="mono">02 / REFERENCE</span><h3>Eroded labels</h3><p>Six semantic classes; boundary pixels outside the scored reference remain excluded.</p></li>
      <li><span class="mono">03 / MODEL</span><h3>Recorded predictions</h3><p>DINOv3 RGB and PSPNet RGB outputs from checkpoints bound in the figure manifest.</p></li>
      <li><span class="mono">04 / OUTCOME</span><h3>Paired correctness</h3><p>Both-correct, shared-error, disagreement, and model-only-correct states come from the archived paired maps.</p></li>
      <li><span class="mono">05 / MEASURE</span><h3>Confusion counts</h3><p>Exact class-pair counts and scene summaries come from the public evidence registry.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <p class="note journey-note">The featured vegetation-disagreement crop is a targeted hard case: tree and low-vegetation regions have similar appearance, and the recorded models disagree in parts of the crop. The gallery is deterministic, not a random sample, so it does not estimate how often that pattern occurs. <a href={route('evaluation')}>Inspect the full matrix and case notes ↗</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="benchmark-section">
    <div class="wrap benchmark-grid">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Measured evidence</p><h2>How the recipes scored.</h2><p>The DINOv3 RGB and PSPNet RGB pair share the recorded evaluation setup. DINOv2 and SAM are historical recipe comparisons. All four entries use the same scene IDs and scored class supports.</p><a class="text-link" href={route('evaluation')}>Inspect the benchmark ↗</a></div>
      <div class="instrument bars" data-benchmark>
        <div class="segmented" aria-label="Benchmark metric"><button aria-pressed="true" data-metric="miou">Mean IoU</button><button aria-pressed="false" data-metric="oa">Overall accuracy</button></div>
        {modelKeys.map((key) => { const model = benchmark.models[key]; const m = metrics(model.aggregate_confusion_matrix);
          return <div class="bar-row" data-miou={m.miou} data-oa={m.oa}><span>{model.display_name}</span><strong>{percent(m.miou)}</strong><div><i style={`--value:${m.miou * 100}%`}></i></div></div>;
        })}
        <div class="axis"><span>0%</span><span>50%</span><span>100%</span></div>
        <p class="note">{best.total.toLocaleString('en-US')} scored pixels · eroded reference · six classes</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap exhibits">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> The research lab</p><h2>Choose an exhibit.</h2><p>Each explorer keeps measured evidence, educational diagrams, and private local data distinct.</p></div>
    <div class="exhibit-list">{exhibits.map(([id, title, body, path]) =>
      <a href={route(path)}><span class="mono">{id}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{body}</p><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    )}</div>
  </section>
</Atlas>
<style>
  .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .72fr) minmax(0, 1.28fr); gap: clamp(22px, 3.2vw, 52px); }
  .hero-copy { align-self: center; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(3.7rem, 6.9vw, 7rem); }
  .hero-plate { min-width: 0; padding: .45rem; background: var(--navy); border: 1px solid var(--dark-rule); box-shadow: 0 20px 50px #0b22391c; }
  .hero-caveat { margin-top: 1.35rem; max-width: 34rem; color: #687780; font-size: .78rem; }
  .research-intro { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .65fr 1.35fr; gap: 2rem; align-items: start; padding-block: clamp(46px, 6.6vw, 96px) 1rem; }
  .research-intro h2 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.3rem); margin-bottom: .45em; }
  .research-intro p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width: 54rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .journey { padding-top: clamp(42px, 5vw, 72px); }
  .scene-stages { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.1rem; padding: 0; margin: 2rem 0 0; list-style: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .scene-stages li { padding-top: .8rem; border-top: 2px solid transparent; }
  .scene-stages li:first-child { border-color: var(--amber); }
  .scene-stages h3 { margin: .8rem 0 .45rem; font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.7vw, 1.5rem); }
  .scene-stages p { color: var(--muted); font-size: .84rem; }
  .scene-stages .mono { color: var(--ocean); font-size: .62rem; }
  .journey-note { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .journey-note a { color: #245f74; font-weight: 600; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .hero-copy { max-width: 48rem; }
    .hero-plate { max-width: 760px; }
    .scene-stages { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .scene-stages li { padding-bottom: .5rem; }
    .research-intro { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: .6rem; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .scene-stages { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: .4rem; }
    .scene-stages li { padding: .65rem 0 .45rem .85rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--rule); border-top: 0; }
    .scene-stages li:first-child { border-left-color: var(--amber); }
    .scene-stages h3 { margin: .35rem 0; }
  }
</style>
<script>
  import { percent } from '../scripts/metrics.mjs';
  import { restore, share } from '../scripts/state.mjs';
  const chart = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-benchmark]')!;
  const toggles = Array.from(chart.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-metric]'));
  restore(chart);
  for (const button of toggles) button.addEventListener('click', () => {
    for (const item of toggles) item.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(item === button));
    for (const bar of chart.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.bar-row')) {
      const value = Number(bar.dataset[button.dataset.metric!]);
      bar.querySelector('strong')!.textContent = percent(value);
      bar.querySelector('i')!.style.setProperty('--value', `${value * 100}%`);
    }
    share(chart);
  });
</script>
